From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 23:09:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: the shared-expert SwiGLU hidden inside the routed
 gate+up matvec (+1.5% decode)

After 0047's node reorder the shared-expert SwiGLU sits immediately after the
routed gate+up MUL_MAT_ID, and the two are completely independent: the SwiGLU
reads only the shared-expert gate/up pair, computed several dispatches earlier.
It is 2 workgroups and 1.4 us, 40 times a decoded token, and almost all of that
is launch latency - the same shape as 0046's topk guest, and the same reason it
is free: the predictor for a tiny guest is CAPACITY, not the time ratio. A
handful of blocks joining 4096 never competes for the host's bandwidth.

The body (GLU + the folded q8_1 quantize, 0010) is warp-local: no shared memory,
no __syncthreads, and its two reductions are warp_reduce_*<QK8_1=32> over 32
CONSECUTIVE elements of a flat index. So it stays bit-identical under any block
shape whose thread count is a multiple of the warp size, and it can simply run
as one extra blockIdx.x slice of the routed matvec's grid, indexing its own
blocks off the channel axis it has no use for. The body moved into
glu-quant-body.cuh so the standalone kernel and the guest run the same
statements, exactly as 0046 did with topk-moe-body.cuh.

The q8_1 destination is registered before the launch, so if the host's launch
geometry cannot carry the guest the fallback runs the standalone kernel into
that same buffer rather than leaving the consumer an unwritten cache entry.
Guest writes are checked disjoint from every host read and host write (0045's
lesson - the two halves run in one kernel with no ordering between them), and
the intermediate nodes go through the usual hoist check.

Census: 641.1 -> 601.1 dispatches/token, exactly -40.0, unary_gated_op_quant
2800 -> 1400 per 35 tokens (the GDN one remains). Stacked on 0047 against a
binary built from 0047's parent commit: tg128 159.70 vs 153.38, 4/4 separated,
+4.12% for the pair; pp512 flat. Decode-path perplexity unchanged.

GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_GLU_COLAUNCH=0 restores the separate launch.
